            {
              "text": "In Perth’s prestige property landscape, several boutique agencies distinguish themselves through **editorial-grade video campaigns, digital-first social marketing, and an authentic appreciation for design and architecture**. \n\n---\n\n### 1. ZSA ZSA Property\n* **The Vibe:** High-end architectural curation, editorial, and design-led.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Founded by Danielle Geagea, ZSA ZSA Property has carved out what is arguably the most distinct architectural niche in Western Australia. The agency frequently lists iconic mid-century modern residences (including celebrated works by Iwan Iwanoff) as well as striking contemporary projects designed by top studios like State of Kin, Klopper & Davis, and Whispering Smith.\n* **Marketing & Video Style:** Rather than standard walkthroughs, they produce episodic-style cinematic pieces (such as their *Design Stories* series) focusing heavily on materiality, natural light, and the narrative behind the architect and builder. Their Instagram feed reads like *The Local Project* or *Est Living*, prioritizing aesthetics and genuine architectural storytelling.\n\n### 2. DUET Property Group\n* **The Vibe:** Sleek, contemporary Western Suburbs prestige.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Operating primarily across Nedlands, Dalkeith, Claremont, and Cottesloe, DUET combines high-volume luxury sales with a very sharp, polished boutique identity. They regularly handle significant modernist and architect-designed homes as well as luxury, boutique multi-residential developments (e.g., collaborating with DKO Architects).\n* **Marketing & Video Style:** DUET’s branding is clean, minimalist, and luxury-oriented. Their campaigns rely on high-production 4K cinematic films, targeted paid Meta (Instagram/Facebook) campaigns, and snappy vertical short-form reels that highlight lifestyle and architectural details.\n\n### 3. White House Property Partners\n* **The Vibe:** Refined, design-conscious, and community-connected coastal/heritage luxury.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Based around Fremantle and the riverside Western Suburbs, White House Property Partners (led by Stefanie Dobro) is renowned for marketing homes with character, from mid-century renovations and heritage restorations to cutting-edge contemporary builds. \n* **Marketing & Video Style:** They are widely recognized across WA real estate circles for their social media presence. Their marketing focuses on lifestyle, warmth, and aesthetic nuance. Rather than transactional ads, their videos and imagery feel editorial, showcasing how the space feels to live in through beautiful twilight captures, drone videography, and stylized walk-throughs.\n\n### 4. Space Real Estate\n* **The Vibe:** Trophy coastal estates and architect-designed beachfront living.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Based in Cottesloe, Space Real Estate has long represented some of the most striking architectural masterpieces along Perth’s coastline (Cottesloe, City Beach, Swanbourne, and Peppermint Grove). They specialize in multi-million-dollar custom builds, concrete modernist homes, and unique coastal architecture.\n* **Marketing & Video Style:** Space leans heavily into cinematic, high-budget property trailers. Their video productions use motion work, sweeping coastal aerials, and high-impact soundtracking to position properties as once-in-a-generation collector items.\n\n### 5. Haiven Property\n* **The Vibe:** Energetic, hyper-modern, and social-first.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Formed by top-tier agents with a modern mandate, Haiven Property handles a large portfolio of custom luxury homes in coastal and near-city enclaves (such as City Beach, Trigg, and South Perth). \n* **Marketing & Video Style:** Haiven is built around digital speed and reach. They are aggressive early adopters of vertical video (TikTok and Instagram Reels), high-end drone sequences, and agent-led spotlight tours that generate substantial viral engagement and direct buyer inquiries from outside traditional property portals.\n\n---\n\n### What to Look For in Their Campaigns\nWhen reviewing these agencies for an architectural property, note the traits that distinguish their campaigns from standard corporate franchises:\n* **The Narrative Approach:** Instead of simply listing room dimensions, the copy and script credit the architects, builders, and specific materials (e.g., rammed earth, off-form concrete, timber joinery).\n* **Editorial Production Teams:** They commonly engage Perth’s premier creative studios (such as *Crib Creative* or dedicated architectural cinematographers) rather than generic real estate media suppliers.\n* **Digital Distribution Beyond Portals:** While listings still appear on REA and Domain, up to 40% of their top-of-funnel engagement is driven through micro-targeted Meta campaigns, Instagram Reels, and private VIP social previews.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
